# The Content-Security-Policy in vercel.json pins SHA-256 hashes of the inline
# <script> blocks in the .html files. A hash covers the exact bytes the browser
# receives, so a CRLF/LF change to any of these files silently invalidates it
# and the pages stop working. Pin them to LF — which is what Vercel's Linux
# build already checks out — so that can never drift.
# See scripts/compute-csp-hashes.js.
*.html text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
